{"sha":"aa262928595d431bfee7914cb7d9d79197f887a2","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0NTM4MzczMTphYTI2MjkyODU5NWQ0MzFiZmVlNzkxNGNiN2Q5ZDc5MTk3Zjg4N2Ey","commit":{"author":{"name":"Halil Pasic","email":"pasic@linux.vnet.ibm.com","date":"2017-03-02T18:13:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"Michael S. Tsirkin","email":"mst@redhat.com","date":"2017-03-28T23:35:23Z"},"message":"event_notifier: prevent accidental use after close\n\nLet's set the handles to the underlying facilities to their extremal\nvalue so no accidental misuse can happen, and to make it obvious that the\nnotifier is dysfunctional. E.g. if we just close an fd but do not touch\nthe int holding the fd eventually a read/write could succeed again when\nthe fd gets reused, and corrupt the file addressed by the fd.\n\nSigned-off-by: Halil Pasic <pasic@linux.vnet.ibm.com>\nReviewed-by: Stefan Hajnoczi <stefanha@redhat.com>\nReviewed-by: Michael S. Tsirkin <mst@redhat.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael S. Tsirkin <mst@redhat.com>","tree":{"sha":"8dfbad003754d9e9707f272609c656c248ab842a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qemu/qemu/git/trees/8dfbad003754d9e9707f272609c656c248ab842a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qemu/qemu/git/commits/aa262928595d431bfee7914cb7d9d79197f887a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qemu/qemu/commits/aa262928595d431bfee7914cb7d9d79197f887a2","html_url":"https://github.com/qemu/qemu/commit/aa262928595d431bfee7914cb7d9d79197f887a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qemu/qemu/commits/aa262928595d431bfee7914cb7d9d79197f887a2/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"mstsirkin","id":1062804,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjI4MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1062804?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mstsirkin","html_url":"https://github.com/mstsirkin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mstsirkin/followers","following_url